      "id": "f40ce66a-fdea-4aa8-a77f-aa72942cc14c",
      "name": "Sticky Note 03a94d06",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        100,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 10 Real-Time Voice Automation Agent\n\naudio or text -> transcription -> intent -> restricted tool -> governance if it changes data -> reply -> verification -> speech -> webhook response.\n\nAudio is optional. A text payload exercises everything downstream of transcription, which is how the pipeline is tested without recording audio.",
        "color": 4,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 240
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f40a2a82-eb50-47bb-a20f-2a0ebf7681b6",
      "name": "Sticky Note 09e66883",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        100,
        640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What this agent is allowed to do\n\nThe tool surface is a **closed registry** of five intents. A name the model invents becomes `unsupported`; it never becomes an attempt to do something undefined.\n\nWhether an intent changes data is declared **in the registry, not by the model**. Those intents go to Governance, and even on approval this workflow **does not execute them** — the approval is recorded for a human. That is what makes a public voice demo safe to point a webhook at.",
        "color": 6,
        "width": 500,
        "height": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "6236bb6c-571a-4e04-8b6e-009089a61eef",
      "name": "Sticky Note 4e3feb97",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        100,
        1040
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Latency is measured per stage\n\nTimestamps are taken at the webhook, after transcription, after intent and after the tool call, so the response reports `transcription_ms`, `intent_ms`, `tool_ms` and the reply/verify/speech tail separately.\n\nA single total would hide the fact that a voice agent usually spends its budget in speech-to-text and text-to-speech rather than in the parts that feel like the \"AI\".",
        "color": 3,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 260
      }
    }
  ],
